spec/spec-process-protected-path-policy.md:18:This specification applies to Runtime Settings, task dispatch validation, changed-path inspection, Stage Commit, Stage Push, Task Branch Integration, Startup Reconciliation, Manual Task Merge, and Batch Pull Request handoff.
spec/spec-process-protected-path-policy.md:33:- **Runtime Settings**: The `settings.json` portion of the Runtime Contract.
spec/spec-process-protected-path-policy.md:35:- **Protected Path Policy**: A repository-owned rule that identifies Workspace Repository paths agent work must not modify without explicit authorization.
spec/spec-process-protected-path-policy.md:38:- **Stage Commit**: A commit created after an agent successfully completes a configured stage.
spec/spec-process-protected-path-policy.md:45:- **REQ-001**: The first version MUST store Protected Path Policy in Runtime Settings under Git Policy as `git.protectedPaths`.
spec/spec-process-protected-path-policy.md:67:### Runtime Settings Shape
spec/spec-process-protected-path-policy.md:69:The first version MUST use `git.protectedPaths` as the canonical Runtime Settings shape. The policy is omitted by default for backward compatibility. When present, `patterns` is an ordered list of named path patterns, and `authorizationSection` names the human-authored issue section Symphony reads before dispatch.
spec/spec-process-protected-path-policy.md:98:- Leading `/` is ignored during matching but SHOULD NOT be used in Runtime Settings.
spec/spec-process-protected-path-policy.md:136:Batch Pull Request handoff MUST treat unresolved protected-path attention the same way it treats unresolved orchestration attention: no Batch Branch Push and no Batch Pull Request creation until the attention is resolved outside the agent retry loop.
spec/spec-process-protected-path-policy.md:168:- **AC-001**: Given a policy protecting `bin/symphony.js`, When an agent modifies that file without authorization, Then Symphony pauses the task in Human Attention Status before Stage Commit.
spec/spec-process-protected-path-policy.md:169:- **AC-002**: Given an issue contains `path:bin/symphony.js` in the configured authorization section, When an agent modifies that path, Then Symphony allows normal Stage Commit behavior.
spec/spec-process-protected-path-policy.md:179:- **Test Data Management**: Temporary Workspace Repository fixtures with Git worktrees, policy settings, and synthetic issues.
spec/spec-process-protected-path-policy.md:195:Self-dogfooding requires stronger safeguards than prompt instructions. Routine agent tasks should not accidentally change package entrypoints, release workflows, packaged binary scripts, or other sensitive files. A repository-owned Protected Path Policy makes those safeguards explicit and enforceable before commits and integrations.
spec/spec-process-protected-path-policy.md:197:Runtime Settings is the preferred first storage location because it keeps policy configuration in the Runtime Contract and avoids introducing a new file format before the matching and authorization semantics are stable.
spec/spec-process-protected-path-policy.md:212:- **INF-001**: Runtime Home - Stores Runtime Settings and Runtime State.
docs/adr/0006-browser-local-audio-notifications.md:21:Audio Notifications remain browser-local and opt-in. Symphony does not add backend notification events, Runtime Settings, audio assets, or notification history for this behavior.
apps/backend/lib/runtime_policy.ml:1:type action = Serve_readiness_state | Run_orchestrator
