apps/backend/lib/runtime_policy.ml:4:  match readiness_gaps with
apps/backend/lib/runtime_policy.ml:5:  | _ :: _ -> Serve_readiness_state
spec/spec-tool-stage-context-command.md:7:tags: [tool, agent-context, runtime-settings, issue-40]
spec/spec-tool-stage-context-command.md:20:This specification covers Runtime Settings, validation, command execution, stdin JSON, temp-file JSON, stdout injection, warnings, and tests.
spec/spec-tool-stage-context-command.md:32:- **Agent Worktree**: The per-task Git worktree used to run agent work.
spec/spec-tool-stage-context-command.md:39:- **REQ-003**: `cwd` MUST be constrained to `workspaceRepositoryRoot` or `agentWorktree`.
spec/spec-tool-stage-context-command.md:53:### Runtime Settings Shape
spec/spec-tool-stage-context-command.md:58:    "command": [".symphony/scripts/agent-context.sh"],
spec/spec-tool-stage-context-command.md:59:    "cwd": "agentWorktree",
spec/spec-tool-stage-context-command.md:79:  "agentWorktree": "/path/to/workspace/.symphony/workspaces/task-40",
spec/spec-tool-stage-context-command.md:80:  "taskBranch": "symphony/task/40-run-a-stage-context-command-before-agent-launch"
spec/spec-tool-stage-context-command.md:91:- **AC-006**: Given invalid cwd, When readiness is checked, Then a Readiness Gap names the invalid setting.
spec/spec-tool-stage-context-command.md:119:- **PLT-001**: OCaml backend - Parses settings and executes commands.
docs/adr/0020-task-pull-request-mode.md:7:In `task` mode, Symphony opens or reuses a Task Pull Request when a task moves to the review status. The pull request head is the task's Task Branch and the base is the configured Pull Request Base Branch. Because the head is the Task Branch, Symphony may run from `main` with `pullRequest.baseBranch` also set to `main`; the self-target readiness gap applies only to Batch Pull Request mode.
