docs/adr/0021-agent-harness-runtime-settings.md:1:# Agent Harness Runtime Settings
docs/adr/0021-agent-harness-runtime-settings.md:9:Personal Symphony currently treats Codex as the only concrete non-interactive launch path. Runtime Settings expose a `codex` block, the backend renders `codex exec` commands, timeout handling reads from Codex settings, and Stage Goal Handoff depends on Codex `/goal` behavior.
docs/adr/0021-agent-harness-runtime-settings.md:15:Runtime Settings will introduce named Agent Harness definitions. Each Agent Harness has a `kind`, `command`, `model`, `reasoningEffort`, `turnTimeoutMs`, `readTimeoutMs`, and `stallTimeoutMs`.
docs/adr/0021-agent-harness-runtime-settings.md:17:`kind: "codex"` and `kind: "pi"` are distinct harness implementations. Symphony must not infer harness behavior only from the command string.
docs/adr/0021-agent-harness-runtime-settings.md:19:The legacy Runtime Settings `codex` block remains supported as a backwards-compatible Codex Harness. Existing Workspace Repositories that define only the legacy `codex` block continue to run without migration. When both `agents.codex` and the legacy `codex` block are present, `agents.codex` is canonical and the legacy block is ignored for that harness.
docs/adr/0021-agent-harness-runtime-settings.md:21:Stage Agent mappings continue using their existing `agent` identifier to select the named Agent Harness. If a Stage Agent selects an unknown harness, Symphony reports a Readiness Gap instead of dispatching work.
docs/adr/0021-agent-harness-runtime-settings.md:31:Stage Goal Handoff remains Codex Harness-specific for the first PI integration. A Stage Agent that enables Stage Goal Handoff on a non-Codex harness is a Readiness Gap until an equivalent non-Codex goal contract exists.
docs/adr/0021-agent-harness-runtime-settings.md:35:PI can be selected explicitly without pretending to be `codex exec`.
docs/adr/0021-agent-harness-runtime-settings.md:39:Runtime Settings parsing, readiness validation, launch command rendering, timeout handling, and Runtime State naming need implementation review for Codex-specific assumptions.
docs/adr/0021-agent-harness-runtime-settings.md:41:The Runtime Contract changes, so Bootstrap must preserve existing user-edited Runtime Settings and create new defaults only when files are missing.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:7:tags: [process, runtime-settings, scheduler, stage-agents, issue-35]
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:12:This specification defines Stage Concurrency Policy for Personal Symphony. The goal is to let a Workspace Repository configure how many agents may run for each Stage Agent while preserving the global `agent.maxConcurrentAgents` cap.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:18:This specification applies to Runtime Settings, scheduler capacity calculation, Ordered Queue admission, dispatch behavior, Runtime State diagnostics, and tests for concurrent Stage Agent execution.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:24:- Keeping idle agents alive when no issue is dispatchable.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:25:- Replacing the global `agent.maxConcurrentAgents` cap.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:32:- **Runtime Settings**: The `settings.json` portion of the Runtime Contract.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:34:- **Stage Concurrency Policy**: A Runtime Settings rule that limits how many agents may run for a specific Stage Agent.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:42:- **REQ-001**: Runtime Settings MUST support a Stage Concurrency Policy on each `stageAgents.stages[]` entry.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:45:- **REQ-004**: The global `agent.maxConcurrentAgents` value MUST remain the maximum total number of running agents.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:49:- **REQ-008**: Invalid zero, negative, non-integer, or non-numeric limits MUST be Runtime Settings validation errors.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:51:- **REQ-010**: Symphony MUST NOT pre-spawn idle agents.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:52:- **REQ-011**: If one issue is dispatchable for a Stage Agent with limit `2`, Symphony MUST launch only one agent.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:53:- **REQ-012**: When an agent finishes, a later scheduler poll MUST refill only stage slots that have dispatchable issues.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:63:### Runtime Settings Shape
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:69:  "agent": {
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:75:        "agent": "planner",
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:81:        "agent": "engineer",
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:87:        "agent": "reviewer",
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:104:| Stage has no dispatchable issue | Launch no agent for that Stage Agent. |
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:109:- **AC-001**: Given Backlog limit `1`, engineer limit `2`, reviewer limit `2`, and global cap `5`, When all stages have dispatchable issues, Then Symphony can dispatch up to five agents across those Stage Agents.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:110:- **AC-002**: Given engineer limit `2` and one eligible engineer issue, When the scheduler polls, Then Symphony launches one engineer agent.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:111:- **AC-003**: Given stage limits sum to `5` and global cap is `3`, When five issues are eligible, Then Symphony runs no more than three agents total.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:120:- **Test Data Management**: Synthetic issue lists, Stage Agent fixtures, Ordered Queue fixtures, and temporary Runtime Settings files.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:129:- Single issue in a stage with limit `2` launches only one agent.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:130:- Global cap lower than the sum of stage caps still limits total running agents.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:136:The current global concurrency cap is not expressive enough for workflows where different stages should have different throughput. A planner stage may need one agent, while implementation and review stages may safely use more than one.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:150:- **SVC-001**: Codex agent runtime - Receives launched agents for eligible issues.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:154:- **INF-001**: Runtime Home - Stores Runtime Settings and Runtime State.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:196:- A stage limit exceeds the global cap: allow the configuration but the global cap still controls total running agents.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:197:- No dispatchable issue exists for a stage with open capacity: launch no idle agent.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:203:- Runtime Settings validation rejects invalid limits.
spec/spec-process-runtime-documentation-alignment.md:20:The intended audience is maintainers, users installing the CLI Package, contributors developing the Product Repository, and future agents editing documentation.
spec/spec-process-runtime-documentation-alignment.md:34:- **Runtime Settings**: The `settings.json` portion of the Runtime Contract.
spec/spec-process-runtime-documentation-alignment.md:44:- **REQ-001**: `README.md` MUST explain the current user path: install the CLI Package, run Bootstrap from a Workspace Repository root, configure Runtime Settings, store secrets only in Local Environment, and run Symphony.
spec/spec-process-runtime-documentation-alignment.md:46:- **REQ-003**: `README.md` MUST document current Runtime Settings sections for tracker, project statuses, Stage Agents, Git Policy, Stage Commit, Stage Push, Pull Request Policy, and Web Dashboard startup.
spec/spec-process-runtime-documentation-alignment.md:47:- **REQ-004**: `.github/project-tracking.md` MUST describe GitHub Issues + Projects through Runtime Settings, not legacy `WORKFLOW.md`.
spec/spec-process-runtime-documentation-alignment.md:102:- **AC-003**: Given tracker documentation, When it references active runtime configuration, Then it points to Runtime Settings instead of legacy `WORKFLOW.md`.
spec/spec-process-runtime-documentation-alignment.md:131:The current domain model has moved from legacy `WORKFLOW.md` language to a Runtime Contract under `.symphony/`. Documentation must follow that product language so users, maintainers, and agents do not conflate Product Repository source code with Workspace Repository runtime operation.
spec/spec-architecture-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md:7:tags: [architecture, agent-context, runtime-contract, issue-37]
spec/spec-architecture-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md:18:The purpose is to define domain language and architecture boundaries before implementation changes Runtime Settings, Runtime State, Agent Prompt composition, or Runtime Home diagnostics.
spec/spec-architecture-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md:34:- **Runtime Settings**: The `.symphony/settings.json` portion of the Runtime Contract.
spec/spec-architecture-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md:36:- **Agent Prompt**: The rendered task instruction sent to an agent.
spec/spec-architecture-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md:37:- **Stage Goal Handoff**: A stage-specific Codex handoff that sets a Codex goal before the normal Agent Prompt.
spec/spec-architecture-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md:38:- **Agent Context Snapshot**: A bounded, deterministic context section generated by the Symphony launch harness before agent launch or retry.
spec/spec-architecture-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md:46:- **REQ-004**: Agent Context Snapshot MUST coexist with Stage Goal Handoff.
spec/spec-architecture-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md:47:- **REQ-005**: Runtime Settings MUST own operator-configurable context behavior.
spec/spec-architecture-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md:62:| Enablement and limits | Runtime Settings | User-editable Runtime Contract. |
spec/spec-architecture-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md:76:- **AC-003**: Given Stage Goal Handoff is enabled, When Agent Context Snapshot is enabled, Then both mechanisms remain distinct and ordered.
spec/spec-architecture-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md:90:`codex-loop` uses Codex lifecycle hooks for continuation. Symphony already owns agent launch, Agent Worktrees, prompt writing, retries, and Runtime State. Therefore, the transferable design is harness-level bounded context generation, not global hook installation.
spec/spec-architecture-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md:105:- **PLT-001**: OCaml backend - Owns settings parsing, prompt composition, and orchestration.
spec/spec-architecture-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md:114:Stage Goal Handoff content, when enabled
spec/spec-architecture-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md:123:- Missing context settings means context behavior remains disabled.
