spec/spec-architecture-agent-harness-runtime-settings.md:45:- **Runtime Settings**: The `settings.json` portion of the Runtime Contract.
spec/spec-architecture-agent-harness-runtime-settings.md:46:- **Stage Agent**: A Runtime Settings mapping from project statuses to a named agent instruction file, Agent Harness selection, and optional stage behavior.
spec/spec-architecture-agent-harness-runtime-settings.md:47:- **Agent Harness**: A named Runtime Settings launch configuration that tells Symphony which non-interactive agent tool to run for a Stage Agent.
spec/spec-architecture-agent-harness-runtime-settings.md:53:- **Stage Goal Handoff**: A stage-specific Codex handoff that sends `/goal` before the normal Agent Prompt.
spec/spec-architecture-agent-harness-runtime-settings.md:58:- **REQ-001**: Runtime Settings MUST support a named `agents` object keyed by Agent Harness identifier.
spec/spec-architecture-agent-harness-runtime-settings.md:60:- **REQ-003**: Supported initial harness kinds MUST include `codex` and `pi`.
spec/spec-architecture-agent-harness-runtime-settings.md:61:- **REQ-004**: Existing Runtime Settings that only contain the legacy `codex` block MUST continue to work.
spec/spec-architecture-agent-harness-runtime-settings.md:62:- **REQ-005**: Symphony MUST normalize the legacy `codex` block into the default Codex Harness for internal dispatch behavior.
spec/spec-architecture-agent-harness-runtime-settings.md:63:- **REQ-006**: Stage Agent mappings MUST continue using their existing `agent` field as the selected Agent Harness identifier.
spec/spec-architecture-agent-harness-runtime-settings.md:67:- **REQ-010**: PI stdout and stderr MUST be captured as agent output and Runtime Diagnostics in the same operational locations as existing launches.
spec/spec-architecture-agent-harness-runtime-settings.md:68:- **REQ-011**: Harness-specific timeout settings MUST control turn, read, and stall timeout behavior for that running task.
spec/spec-architecture-agent-harness-runtime-settings.md:70:- **REQ-013**: Stage Goal Handoff enabled on a non-Codex harness MUST produce a Readiness Gap in the first PI integration.
spec/spec-architecture-agent-harness-runtime-settings.md:80:- **GUD-001**: Use Agent Harness, Codex Harness, and PI Harness in docs instead of ambiguous phrases such as "agent command."
spec/spec-architecture-agent-harness-runtime-settings.md:81:- **PAT-001**: Prefer external behavior tests for parsing, readiness validation, command rendering, and launch behavior over private implementation tests.
