     1	---
     2	title: Agent Harness Runtime Settings
     3	version: 1.0
     4	date_created: 2026-05-07
     5	last_updated: 2026-05-07
     6	owner: Product Repository maintainers
     7	tags: [architecture, runtime-contract, agent-harness, pi, issue-59]
     8	---
     9	
    10	# Introduction
    11	
    12	This specification defines the Runtime Contract changes required to support PI as a first-class Agent Harness for Personal Symphony Stage Agents while preserving existing Codex behavior.
    13	
    14	Source issue: [#59 PRD: Add PI as a first-class Stage Agent harness](https://github.com/MatheusBBarni/symphony-orchestrator/issues/59).
    15	
    16	## 1. Purpose & Scope
    17	
    18	The purpose is to define how Workspace Repository operators configure and select non-interactive agent launch tools through Runtime Settings.
    19	
    20	This specification applies to the Product Repository backend implementation, Bootstrap defaults, Runtime Settings parsing, readiness validation, launch command rendering, and tests.
    21	
    22	In scope:
    23	
    24	- Add PI as a first-class configurable Agent Harness.
    25	- Preserve the legacy Runtime Settings `codex` block.
    26	- Allow Codex and PI harnesses to coexist.
    27	- Keep existing Agent Worktree, Task Branch, Agent Prompt, Stage Commit, Stage Push, retry, and status transition behavior.
    28	- Keep Stage Goal Handoff Codex Harness-specific in the first PI integration.
    29	
    30	Out of scope:
    31	
    32	- Claude Code integration.
    33	- PI RPC mode.
    34	- PI session resume or fork support.
    35	- PI-specific structured usage accounting.
    36	- Cross-harness Stage Goal Handoff.
    37	- Task Branch cleanup, auto-merge, tracker model, npm package, or packaged-binary behavior changes.
    38	
    39	## 2. Definitions
    40	
    41	- **Workspace Repository**: The repository where a user runs Personal Symphony and where runtime configuration and state are created.
    42	- **Product Repository**: The repository that contains the Personal Symphony source code.
    43	- **Runtime Home**: The `.symphony/` directory that contains Personal Symphony configuration and runtime-owned files for a Workspace Repository.
    44	- **Runtime Contract**: Repository-owned files inside the Runtime Home that define Personal Symphony behavior.
    45	- **Runtime Settings**: The `settings.json` portion of the Runtime Contract.
    46	- **Stage Agent**: A Runtime Settings mapping from project statuses to a named agent instruction file, Agent Harness selection, and optional stage behavior.
    47	- **Agent Harness**: A named Runtime Settings launch configuration that tells Symphony which non-interactive agent tool to run for a Stage Agent.
    48	- **Codex Harness**: An Agent Harness whose launch semantics target Codex non-interactive execution.
    49	- **PI Harness**: An Agent Harness whose launch semantics target PI non-interactive execution.
    50	- **Agent Prompt**: The `prompt.md` Runtime Contract content rendered with issue and stage context for a dispatched task.
    51	- **Agent Worktree**: An Agent Workspace backed by a Git worktree for one dispatched task.
    52	- **Task Branch**: A Git branch created from the Loop-Start Branch for one dispatched task.
    53	- **Stage Goal Handoff**: A stage-specific Codex handoff that sends `/goal` before the normal Agent Prompt.
    54	- **Readiness Gap**: A configuration or environment problem that prevents dispatch while still allowing operator inspection.
    55	
    56	## 3. Requirements, Constraints & Guidelines
    57	
    58	- **REQ-001**: Runtime Settings MUST support a named `agents` object keyed by Agent Harness identifier.
    59	- **REQ-002**: Each Agent Harness MUST define `kind`, `command`, `model`, `reasoningEffort`, `turnTimeoutMs`, `readTimeoutMs`, and `stallTimeoutMs`.
    60	- **REQ-003**: Supported initial harness kinds MUST include `codex` and `pi`.
    61	- **REQ-004**: Existing Runtime Settings that only contain the legacy `codex` block MUST continue to work.
    62	- **REQ-005**: Symphony MUST normalize the legacy `codex` block into the default Codex Harness for internal dispatch behavior.
    63	- **REQ-006**: Stage Agent mappings MUST continue using their existing `agent` field as the selected Agent Harness identifier.
    64	- **REQ-007**: PI command rendering MUST replace `<model>` and `<reasoning>` tokens.
    65	- **REQ-008**: The default PI command MUST be `pi --model <model> --thinking <reasoning> --print --no-session`.
    66	- **REQ-009**: PI dispatch MUST pass the rendered Agent Prompt through a PI-supported non-interactive input path.
    67	- **REQ-010**: PI stdout and stderr MUST be captured as agent output and Runtime Diagnostics in the same operational locations as existing launches.
    68	- **REQ-011**: Harness-specific timeout settings MUST control turn, read, and stall timeout behavior for that running task.
    69	- **REQ-012**: Missing harness definitions, unknown harness kinds, blank commands, blank models, and blank reasoning effort values MUST produce Readiness Gaps.
    70	- **REQ-013**: Stage Goal Handoff enabled on a non-Codex harness MUST produce a Readiness Gap in the first PI integration.
    71	- **REQ-014**: Codex command rendering MUST preserve existing legacy command behavior.
    72	- **REQ-015**: Agent Prompt composition MUST remain consistent across Codex and PI harnesses.
    73	- **REQ-016**: Stage Commit, Stage Push, retry, Human Attention Status, Agent Worktree, and Task Branch behavior MUST remain harness-independent.
    74	- **REQ-017**: Runtime State names and dashboard labels SHOULD be reviewed for misleading Codex-specific terminology before exposing PI runs.
    75	- **CON-001**: The implementation MUST NOT change Task Branch cleanup or auto-merge defaults.
    76	- **CON-002**: The implementation MUST NOT replace the GitHub Issues + Projects tracker model.
    77	- **CON-003**: The implementation MUST NOT change npm package files, `bin/symphony.js`, or packaged-binary behavior.
    78	- **CON-004**: Bootstrap MUST preserve existing user-edited Runtime Contract files.
    79	- **SEC-001**: Documentation and examples MUST NOT include secret values, token values, webhook URLs, or local `.env` contents.
    80	- **GUD-001**: Use Agent Harness, Codex Harness, and PI Harness in docs instead of ambiguous phrases such as "agent command."
    81	- **PAT-001**: Prefer external behavior tests for parsing, readiness validation, command rendering, and launch behavior over private implementation tests.
    82	
    83	## 4. Interfaces & Data Contracts
    84	
    85	### Runtime Settings Shape
    86	
    87	```json
    88	{
    89	  "agents": {
    90	    "codex": {
    91	      "kind": "codex",
    92	      "command": "codex exec",
    93	      "model": "gpt-5.5",
    94	      "reasoningEffort": "medium",
    95	      "turnTimeoutMs": 3600000,
    96	      "readTimeoutMs": 5000,
    97	      "stallTimeoutMs": 300000
    98	    },
    99	    "pi": {
   100	      "kind": "pi",
   101	      "command": "pi --model <model> --thinking <reasoning> --print --no-session",
   102	      "model": "openai/gpt-5.5",
   103	      "reasoningEffort": "medium",
   104	      "turnTimeoutMs": 3600000,
   105	      "readTimeoutMs": 5000,
   106	      "stallTimeoutMs": 300000
   107	    }
   108	  },
   109	  "stageAgents": {
   110	    "stages": [
   111	      {
   112	        "states": ["Todo"],
   113	        "agent": "pi"
   114	      }
   115	    ]
   116	  }
   117	}
   118	```
   119	
   120	### Legacy Runtime Settings Compatibility
   121	
   122	```json
   123	{
   124	  "codex": {
   125	    "command": "codex exec",
   126	    "model": "gpt-5.5",
   127	    "reasoningEffort": "medium"
   128	  }
   129	}
   130	```
   131	
   132	The legacy shape MUST behave as if `agents.codex` exists with `kind: "codex"` and default timeout values.
   133	
   134	If both `agents.codex` and the legacy `codex` block are present, `agents.codex` MUST be canonical and the legacy `codex` block MUST be ignored for that harness. The legacy block is only a compatibility fallback when `agents.codex` is absent.
   135	
   136	### Agent Harness Fields
   137	
   138	| Field | Required | Description |
   139	| --- | --- | --- |
   140	| `kind` | Yes | Harness implementation discriminator. Supported values are `codex` and `pi`. |
   141	| `command` | Yes | Shell command template used for non-interactive launch. |
   142	| `model` | Yes | Harness model identifier. PI values may include provider prefixes. |
   143	| `reasoningEffort` | Yes | Harness reasoning or thinking level. |
   144	| `turnTimeoutMs` | Yes | Maximum elapsed time for one agent turn. |
   145	| `readTimeoutMs` | Yes | Polling sleep chunk used while reading agent output. |
   146	| `stallTimeoutMs` | Yes | Maximum elapsed time without stdout or stderr growth. |
   147	
   148	## 5. Acceptance Criteria
   149	
   150	- **AC-001**: Given legacy Runtime Settings with only `codex`, When Symphony parses settings, Then the default Codex Harness is available and existing Codex launch command rendering is unchanged.
   151	- **AC-002**: Given Runtime Settings with `agents.codex` and `agents.pi`, When a Stage Agent mapping selects `pi`, Then Symphony dispatches that task through the PI Harness.
   152	- **AC-003**: Given a PI Harness command containing `<model>` and `<reasoning>`, When Symphony renders the launch command, Then both tokens are replaced with shell-safe configured values.
   153	- **AC-004**: Given a Stage Agent references an unknown Agent Harness, When readiness is evaluated, Then a Readiness Gap identifies the missing harness.
   154	- **AC-005**: Given an Agent Harness has an unknown `kind`, blank `command`, blank `model`, or blank `reasoningEffort`, When readiness is evaluated, Then a Readiness Gap identifies the invalid field.
   155	- **AC-006**: Given a PI Harness Stage Agent has Stage Goal Handoff enabled, When readiness is evaluated, Then Symphony reports a non-Codex goal handoff Readiness Gap.
   156	- **AC-007**: Given a Codex Harness Stage Agent has Stage Goal Handoff enabled and Codex goal support is configured, When readiness is evaluated, Then existing Codex goal readiness behavior remains valid.
   157	- **AC-008**: Given a PI-launched task exits successfully with code changes, When stage completion runs, Then existing Stage Commit, Stage Push, status transition, and Task Branch behavior applies.
   158	- **AC-009**: Given Bootstrap runs in a Workspace Repository with existing `.symphony/settings.json`, When PI support exists in the Product Repository, Then Bootstrap does not overwrite that file.
   159	- **AC-010**: Given Runtime Settings define both `agents.codex` and the legacy `codex` block, When Symphony parses settings, Then `agents.codex` is used for the Codex Harness and the legacy block is ignored.
   160	
   161	## 6. Test Automation Strategy
   162	
   163	- **Test Levels**: Backend unit and integration-style tests using temporary Workspace Repository fixtures.
   164	- **Frameworks**: OCaml Alcotest through `pnpm test`.
   165	- **Test Data Management**: Use temporary Runtime Home and fake agent commands that write predictable stdout, stderr, and prompt input.
   166	- **CI/CD Integration**: Run focused backend tests after touching configuration or launch modules; run `pnpm test` before merging implementation.
   167	- **Coverage Requirements**: Cover Runtime Settings parsing, legacy compatibility, command rendering, readiness validation, Stage Goal Handoff gating, and launch output capture.
   168	- **Performance Testing**: Not required for the first PI integration.
   169	
   170	## 7. Rationale & Context
   171	
   172	Codex is currently embedded as the only launch abstraction. PI support should not be modeled as a special Codex command because PI has different command-line semantics, model naming, and unsupported goal behavior. A named Agent Harness separates Stage Agent selection from concrete command rendering and makes future harness kinds possible without changing the Stage Agent mapping structure again.
   173	
   174	## 8. Dependencies & External Integrations
   175	
   176	### External Systems
   177	
   178	- **EXT-001**: GitHub Issues + Projects - Supplies issue metadata and project status transitions.
   179	- **EXT-002**: Git - Supplies Agent Worktree and Task Branch isolation.
   180	
   181	### Third-Party Services
   182	
   183	- **SVC-001**: Codex CLI - Required for Codex Harness dispatch.
   184	- **SVC-002**: PI CLI - Required for PI Harness dispatch.
   185	
   186	### Infrastructure Dependencies
   187	
   188	- **INF-001**: Runtime Home - Stores Runtime Contract, Runtime State, Agent Worktrees, and Runtime Diagnostics.
   189	
   190	### Technology Platform Dependencies
   191	
   192	- **PLT-001**: OCaml backend - Owns Runtime Settings parsing, readiness validation, orchestration, launch, and output capture.
   193	- **PLT-002**: Shell-compatible command execution - Required for existing command template behavior.
   194	
   195	### Compliance Dependencies
   196	
   197	- **COM-001**: ADR coverage - Required because Agent Harness changes Runtime Contract semantics.
   198	- **COM-002**: Secret handling - Documentation and tests must avoid committed token values.
   199	
   200	## 9. Examples & Edge Cases
   201	
   202	### PI Command Rendering
   203	
   204	```text
   205	Input command:
   206	pi --model <model> --thinking <reasoning> --print --no-session
   207	
   208	model:
   209	openai/gpt-5.5
   210	
   211	reasoningEffort:
   212	medium
   213	
   214	Rendered command:
   215	pi --model 'openai/gpt-5.5' --thinking 'medium' --print --no-session
   216	```
   217	
   218	### Edge Cases
   219	
   220	- A Workspace Repository has no `agents` object and has a legacy `codex` block: Symphony uses the legacy Codex Harness.
   221	- A Workspace Repository defines both `codex` and `agents.codex`: Symphony uses `agents.codex` as the canonical Codex Harness and ignores the legacy block.
   222	- A Stage Agent selects `pi` but `agents.pi` is missing: readiness blocks dispatch.
   223	- A PI command omits `<model>` and `<reasoning>`: the command is allowed only when non-empty, but no automatic PI argument injection is required beyond token replacement.
   224	- PI writes useful diagnostics to stderr and exits with non-zero status: Symphony captures stderr and applies existing retry behavior.
   225	
   226	## 10. Implementation Handoff
   227	
   228	Likely backend files:
   229	
   230	- `apps/backend/lib/config.ml` for Runtime Settings parsing, Agent Harness normalization, readiness gaps, Stage Goal Handoff gating, and timeout lookup.
   231	- `apps/backend/lib/orchestrator.ml` for harness-specific command rendering, prompt stdin launch, output capture, and per-running-task timeout selection.
   232	- `apps/backend/lib/runtime_home.ml` only if missing-file Bootstrap defaults are intentionally extended; do not overwrite existing Runtime Contract files.
   233	- `apps/backend/lib/runtime_state.ml` and frontend live-state parsing only if Runtime State naming changes are required after reviewing Codex-specific fields.
   234	- `apps/backend/test/test_backend.ml` for focused Alcotest coverage near existing Runtime Settings, launch command, readiness, and Stage Goal Handoff tests.
   235	
   236	Implementation risks:
   237	
   238	- Accidentally treating `pi` as a Codex-compatible command string instead of a PI Harness kind.
   239	- Applying Stage Goal Handoff readiness globally instead of only to Stage Agents whose selected Agent Harness is a Codex Harness.
   240	- Continuing to read timeout settings from the legacy Codex block for PI-launched tasks.
   241	- Changing Bootstrap defaults in `runtime_home.ml` without preserving Idempotent Bootstrap behavior.
   242	- Renaming Runtime State fields in a way that breaks the Live Dashboard without corresponding parsing updates.
   243	
   244	## 11. Validation Criteria
   245	
   246	- `CONTEXT.md` defines Agent Harness, Codex Harness, and PI Harness.
   247	- An ADR records the Runtime Contract decision.
   248	- Runtime Settings examples are secret-free.
   249	- Backend tests prove legacy Codex compatibility and PI command rendering.
   250	- Readiness Gaps prevent unsupported Stage Goal Handoff on PI.
   251	- Focused backend tests cover `agents.codex` precedence over the legacy `codex` block.
   252	- `pnpm test` passes after implementation.
   253	
   254	## 12. Related Specifications / Further Reading
   255	
   256	- [Issue #59](https://github.com/MatheusBBarni/symphony-orchestrator/issues/59)
   257	- [CONTEXT.md](../CONTEXT.md)
   258	- [Agent Harness Runtime Settings ADR](../docs/adr/0021-agent-harness-runtime-settings.md)
   259	- [Stage Goal Handoff ADR](../docs/adr/0007-stage-goal-handoff.md)
     1	# Agent Harness Runtime Settings
     2	
     3	## Status
     4	
     5	Accepted
     6	
     7	## Context
     8	
     9	Personal Symphony currently treats Codex as the only concrete non-interactive launch path. Runtime Settings expose a `codex` block, the backend renders `codex exec` commands, timeout handling reads from Codex settings, and Stage Goal Handoff depends on Codex `/goal` behavior.
    10	
    11	This blocks Workspace Repository operators from selecting PI for specific Stage Agents while preserving the existing Workspace Repository, Runtime Home, Agent Worktree, Task Branch, Agent Prompt, Stage Commit, Stage Push, retry, and status transition behavior.
    12	
    13	## Decision
    14	
    15	Runtime Settings will introduce named Agent Harness definitions. Each Agent Harness has a `kind`, `command`, `model`, `reasoningEffort`, `turnTimeoutMs`, `readTimeoutMs`, and `stallTimeoutMs`.
    16	
    17	`kind: "codex"` and `kind: "pi"` are distinct harness implementations. Symphony must not infer harness behavior only from the command string.
    18	
    19	The legacy Runtime Settings `codex` block remains supported as a backwards-compatible Codex Harness. Existing Workspace Repositories that define only the legacy `codex` block continue to run without migration. When both `agents.codex` and the legacy `codex` block are present, `agents.codex` is canonical and the legacy block is ignored for that harness.
    20	
    21	Stage Agent mappings continue using their existing `agent` identifier to select the named Agent Harness. If a Stage Agent selects an unknown harness, Symphony reports a Readiness Gap instead of dispatching work.
    22	
    23	The first PI Harness uses PI non-interactive print mode with the default command shape:
    24	
    25	```sh
    26	pi --model <model> --thinking <reasoning> --print --no-session
    27	```
    28	
    29	Command rendering replaces `<model>` and `<reasoning>` tokens for all supported harnesses. Codex keeps its existing command rendering behavior for legacy command shapes.
    30	
    31	Stage Goal Handoff remains Codex Harness-specific for the first PI integration. A Stage Agent that enables Stage Goal Handoff on a non-Codex harness is a Readiness Gap until an equivalent non-Codex goal contract exists.
    32	
    33	## Consequences
    34	
    35	PI can be selected explicitly without pretending to be `codex exec`.
    36	
    37	Future Claude Code support can add another Agent Harness kind without changing the Stage Agent mapping model again.
    38	
    39	Runtime Settings parsing, readiness validation, launch command rendering, timeout handling, and Runtime State naming need implementation review for Codex-specific assumptions.
    40	
    41	The Runtime Contract changes, so Bootstrap must preserve existing user-edited Runtime Settings and create new defaults only when files are missing.

